---
source: crates/baml_cli/src/describe_command_tests.rs
expression: output
---
as — Projects a type through an interface, and maps interface fields to class fields.

Syntax:
  // Field mapping inside an implements block.
  interface HasId {
    type Id
    id: Id
  }
  
  class User {
    implements HasId {
      type Id = string
      id as user_id
    }
    full_name: string
    user_id: string
  }
  
  // Associated type projection in a type position.
  type UserId = (User as HasId).Id

Use `(Type as Interface).Assoc` for qualified associated type projection in a type position. Inside an `implements` block, `interface_field as class_field` maps an interface field to a differently named class field. To view a value at one of its interfaces, write `value.upcast<Interface>()` (see `baml describe upcast`); the earlier `as` spelling of that operator was removed and is a compile error (E0098).
